  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">"This book was produced while in residence at the Visual Studies Workshop, Rochester, NY in December 2004. The artist in residence program of the Visual Studies Workshop is supported by funds from the Nimoy Foundation and the National Endowment for the Arts. Digitally printed with HP Indigo technology in the United States of America."--Colophon.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="505" ind1="0" ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Autobiography #5: C(a[e[opening brace]I[closing brace]o]u)P--[Recipe card]--Cups--Things to do: Autobiography #1.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="520" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">"C(a[e[opening brace]I[closing brace]o]u)P : Autobiography #5 combines my parent's small collections with my own, broadening the definition of a self-portrait through generational/genealogical slices. Tea cups my mother displayed in exacting order on a cherry wood hutch her father had crafted complimenet souvenir caps from my travels. Videotapes my father recorded over and over and labeled accordingly are framed by pages from my "to-do" lists (published as Autobiography #1 in 1997) [...]. I chose the "dos-a-dos" form for this book which traditionally binds the two texts together with a common back cover. The two booklets are bound in the representation of wood and yarn, materials which my father and mother chose to express themselves creatively - the book itself being my own mode for obsessive expression (and collection)"--Autobiography #5: C(a[e[opening brace]I[closing brace]o]u)P (first pamphlet).</subfield>
  </datafield>
